Chapter: LensSqlTest
  cites Data chapter Row
  cites Data chapter RelAlgebra
  cites Lens chapter LensModel
  cites Lens chapter LensPlan
  cites Lens chapter LensSql

 Known-answer test for the T-SQL emitter. The model is the star from
 the planner test: orders is the fact, users the dimension table, one
 many-to-one join between them, and the column names carry hyphens on
 purpose so every emitted reference exercises bracket quoting. Each
 query below runs through lens-plan, so the emitter is fed exactly
 the trees the planner builds, and the emitted statement is pinned as
 text.

 The pins cover the planner's whole emission surface. Revenue by city
 is the three-step grain ladder: a GROUP BY at the orders grain
 inside a derived table, an INNER JOIN to users on the join key, and
 a re-aggregation by city, crowned by projection and an ascending
 sort. The fan-out query adds a second measure aggregated at the
 users grain and joined on the full dimension column set. The
 filtered query pushes its predicate inside the derived table under
 the revenue group, where raw-row grain lives. The limited query
 renders TOP inside the projection head. The dimensionless query
 glues two single-row aggregates with CROSS JOIN. The quoted filter
 carries a single quote in its literal and must double it.

 The bucketed queries pin the derive emission. A month-bucketed
 dimension over the order-date column, Unix seconds in a BIGINT,
 emits a derived table that projects the scan's columns and appends
 YEAR times one hundred plus MONTH of DATEADD(second, order-date,
 '19700101') under the alias order-date__month, so the warehouse
 computes exactly the integers the native executor's month encoding
 computes, 202606 for June 2026. The join form groups the home grain
 by user-id and the bucket alias inside the derived table, joins
 users, and re-aggregates by city and the alias, mirroring the
 native plan shape node for node. Both statements below were
 executed against a live LocalDB warehouse seeded with the planner
 test's star and answered the same bucket integers and revenue sums
 the native lens-query-test pins.

Section: The Model

  users-t : LensTable
  users-t = LensTable { name = "users", primary-key = "user-id", grain = "one row per registered user" }

  orders-t : LensTable
  orders-t = LensTable { name = "orders", primary-key = "order-id", grain = "one row per order" }

  orders-to-users : LensJoin
  orders-to-users = LensJoin { from-table = "orders", to-table = "users", on-left = "user-id", on-right = "user-id", cardinality = ManyToOne }

  city-dim : LensDimension
  city-dim = LensDimension { name = "city", table = "users", column = "city", bucket = LbNone }

  product-dim : LensDimension
  product-dim = LensDimension { name = "product", table = "orders", column = "product-id", bucket = LbNone }

  month-dim : LensDimension
  month-dim = LensDimension { name = "order-month", table = "orders", column = "order-date", bucket = LbMonth }

  revenue-measure : LensMeasure
  revenue-measure = LensMeasure {
    name = "revenue",
    table = "orders",
    column = "amount",
    agg = LensAggSum,
    description = "Sum of order amounts in cents."
  }

  credit-measure : LensMeasure
  credit-measure = LensMeasure {
    name = "total-credit",
    table = "users",
    column = "credit-limit",
    agg = LensAggSum,
    description = "Sum of user credit limits in cents. User grain."
  }

  sales-model : LensModel
  sales-model = LensModel {
    name = "sales",
    tables = [users-t, orders-t],
    joins = [orders-to-users],
    dimensions = [city-dim, product-dim, month-dim],
    measures = [revenue-measure, credit-measure]
  }

Section: Queries

  revenue-by-city-q : LensQuery
  revenue-by-city-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  fanout-q : LensQuery
  fanout-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  product-filter : LensFilter
  product-filter = LensFilter { table = "orders", column = "product-id", value = LfInt 1 }

  filtered-q : LensQuery
  filtered-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [product-filter], limit = 0 }

  limited-q : LensQuery
  limited-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 2 }

  no-dim-q : LensQuery
  no-dim-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = [], measures = ["total-credit", "revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  quoted-filter : LensFilter
  quoted-filter = LensFilter { table = "users", column = "city", value = LfText "Coeur d'Alene" }

  quoted-q : LensQuery
  quoted-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [quoted-filter], limit = 0 }

  bucket-q : LensQuery
  bucket-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["order-month"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

  bucket-join-q : LensQuery
  bucket-join-q = LensQuery { lens-name = "sales", dimensions = ["city", "order-month"], measures = ["revenue"], filters = [], limit = 0 }

Section: Rendering

 A planned query renders as its emitted statement; a refused query
 renders its diagnostics so a planner regression is visible here too.

  render-sql : LensQuery -> Text
  render-sql (q) =
    let pr = lens-plan sales-model q
    in if pr.plan-ok == False then "DIAGS: " & lp-render-diags (pr.plan-diags) 0 ""
    else lens-to-tsql (pr.plan-op)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "=== lens sql test: T-SQL emission from planned trees ==="
    print-line-uni "-- revenue by city"
    print-line-uni (render-sql revenue-by-city-q)
    print-line-uni "-- fan-out: credit and revenue by city"
    print-line-uni (render-sql fanout-q)
    print-line-uni "-- filter under the revenue group"
    print-line-uni (render-sql filtered-q)
    print-line-uni "-- limit renders as TOP"
    print-line-uni (render-sql limited-q)
    print-line-uni "-- no dimensions: CROSS JOIN glue"
    print-line-uni (render-sql no-dim-q)
    print-line-uni "-- text literal doubles its quote"
    print-line-uni (render-sql quoted-q)
    print-line-uni "-- month bucket derive"
    print-line-uni (render-sql bucket-q)
    print-line-uni "-- month bucket across the join"
    print-line-uni (render-sql bucket-join-q)
    print-line-uni "lens-sql-test: done"
  end
